 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Added
+
+- Provider credentials can come from a file or a command instead of the environment:
+  `providers.<id>.api_key_file` reads a path (sops-nix and other secret stores) and
+  `providers.<id>.api_key_command` runs a helper such as `pass show`. Both take the first
+  non-blank line, and a configured source that fails falls back to the next one after a warning.
+  See [docs/providers.md](docs/providers.md#custom-providers).
+- `/tree` navigates conversation turns in the same session. Editing an old prompt preserves its
+  descendants, including history left by `/undo`. Branch switches persist immediately, keep the
+  current model selection, and print only a short marker; Ctrl-O shows the selected history. Rows
+  show real ancestry and mark only the current turn. Enter continues after the selected turn;
+  `e` edits its prompt (`Alt-E` while filtering, `/` to search starting with `e`). `s` summarizes
+  the branch being left and carries that summary into the destination as context, so what it tried
+  survives the switch. The summary ends with the files that branch read and changed, collected from
+  its tool calls and carried across earlier branch summaries. Navigation requires session recording and no uncollected background tasks.
+  Pressing Escape at an empty prompt also opens the tree, without affecting Esc during active work.
+
 ### Changed
 
+- Summarization reads only the first 2000 characters of each tool result, marked where it was cut.
+  Command output is usually most of a window, and a summary needs to know what was run rather than
+  reproduce it, so `/compact` and branch summaries no longer pay for the whole dump.
+- Compaction now keeps the newest user turn verbatim after its summary instead of replacing the
+  whole window with prose, so work continues from the exact state it was last in. Set
+  `compact.keep_turns` to keep more turns, or `0` for the previous summarize-everything behavior.
+  The kept tail is capped at a quarter of a known context window, so a turn too large to keep is
+  summarized rather than left to overflow it.
+  See [docs/usage.md](docs/usage.md#context-compaction-and-usage).
 - Prompts are sent without leading blank lines or trailing whitespace, so a paste or Ctrl+G edit
   that ends in a newline no longer echoes as empty rows. The first line keeps its indentation.
   A prompt that is only whitespace sends nothing, and `-p` rejects it as empty.
